summary:
  Starting the MPRIS bridge again forgets which commands were already obeyed,
  so a read of the old file obeys its last key a second time.

history:
  The widget starts the bridge again when it finds it gone and when media
  keys are switched back on, with the same gate and with the poll still
  running. Zeroing the mark there made any line under ten seconds old new
  again for the read that lands before the start has emptied the file. The
  bridge numbers from the clock, so keeping the mark costs nothing.

target:
  package/contents/ui/MprisCommandGate.qml

find:
      function arm(nowMs) {

replace:
      function arm(nowMs) { lastSeq = 0; return;

expect:
  Killed by tests/qml/tst_mpriscommandgate.qml::test_a_new_bridge_does_not_replay_what_the_old_one_said.
  Line-neutral.
